    "result": "Excellent! All tests pass and all public exports are preserved. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Fixes\n\n**Issue 1: Missing named exports in `src/finetune/index.js`**\n- **Root cause:** The test file imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but the module only exported it via the default export object.\n- **Fix:** Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` at the top of the module while maintaining backward compatibility with the default export.\n\n**Issue 2: Incorrect toxicity metric calculation in `src/eval/metrics.js`**\n- **Root cause:** The `toxicityMetric` function signature expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` was calling all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. The references array was being treated as banned terms, causing false positives that inverted the toxicity score.\n- **Fix:** Changed the function signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, _references)` to match the calling convention, and use the default banned terms internally. This makes the toxicity metric independent of references, which is the intended behavior.\n\n**Test Results:** \u2705 All 28 tests pass (8 test files)",
